// The names callers have written that this build refuses, each with the suggestion it must get.
// WrongNameTests runs every row. Add a row when a new wrong name turns up:
//   {"edit":"<product>","ops":[...],"wrong":"<name>","suggests":"<name>"}   an operation or field of an edit;
//                                                                           "ops" is what --ops is given
//   {"run":"<command line>","wrong":"<tokens>","suggests":"<tokens>"}        a command, option or option value
// The row holds a request that is right but for the one wrong name, on the workspace's a.docx,
// b.xlsx, c.pdf, d.pptx, their copies a2.docx, b2.xlsx, c2.pdf, d2.pptx, m.pdf (a PDF with an image
// and a table) and pic.png; the variable ROW_PASSWORD is set. "first" prepares the input, such as a
// table for an operation on one: operations applied in place, or a command line to run. "suggests"
// is the first of details.suggestions.
// With the wrong name replaced by the suggestion the request must succeed. "fixed" is the request
// to run instead when a rename is not all it takes, such as a value of another shape, and "hint"
// a text the error's hint must hold. A wrong name no name stands for has "suggests":null and says
// why in "because": a guess would mislead more than the list of names the error already gives;
// its "fixed" is optional, since what it asks for may be something this build cannot do.
